  "articleBody": "It's super frustrating when your garage floor coating starts peeling or bubbling, right? Often, the root cause comes down to a few common culprits. A big one is improper surface prep. If the concrete wasn't ground or profiled correctly, or if there was leftover residue, that new coating just won't stick. Skipping moisture testing is another huge mistake; moisture pushing up from the slab can absolutely destroy an otherwise good coating. Sometimes, it's also about the product itself—using something that's not durable enough for garage traffic, or not applying the right primer and top coat system. Cold weather during application can also mess with cure times, leading to a weaker bond. If you've tried DIY and it's not holding up, or if your slab has cracks, old coatings, or drainage issues, it's definitely time to bring in a pro. They've got the tools and expertise to properly assess the situation, fix the underlying issues, and get that coating to last. HH Remodeling LLC has seen it all and can help you get a floor that stands the test of time.",
